            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for stubbornness, then the Hindi for eligible."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: बेहद",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बेहद — behad — \"extremely, beyond measure\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "अगर आज भी बेहद गर्मी रही तो स्कूल बंद रहेंगे। agar āj bhī behad garmī rahī to skūl band raheṅge. If it is extremely hot again today, the schools will stay shut."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बेहद (behad) is usually traced to Persian behadd, \"without limit\". It joins Persian be-, \"without\", to Arabic ḥadd, \"a limit\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
            }
          ]
        },
